  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Canon\n\n**Headline finding: there is no test infrastructure anywhere in this repo, and ~90% of `engine/` is unimplemented (`raise NotImplementedError`).** This changes what \"coverage gap\" means here — most of the pipeline has no logic to test yet. I've split the findings accordingly: real gaps (implemented code, zero tests) vs. contract-pinning gaps (stubs that should get tests *now*, TDD-style, so Phase 2/3 implementation has a spec to satisfy).\n\nNo `pytest.ini`/`conftest.py`/`tests/` dir exists despite `pytest>=8.3` being an engine dev-dependency. No `vitest`/`jest`/`@testing-library/*` in `web/package.json` at all.\n\n---\n\n### 0. Test infrastructure gap (blocks everything else)\n\n- **Engine**: `pytest` is declared but unused. Need `engine/tests/__init__.py` + a `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` block in `pyproject.toml` (e.g. `testpaths = [\"tests\"]`).\n- **Web**: no test runner installed. Recommend **Vitest** (fast, ESM/TS-native, pairs well with Next 16 + Zod) plus **@testing-library/react** for the few components with logic (`SeverityMark`, `NavRail`).\n\nPer AGENTS.md § Decision Making, I'm naming this rather than installing it — **want me to add Vitest + Testing Library to `web/devDependencies`?** Nothing below requires that decision; the skeletons work with either Vitest or Jest syntax (near-identical).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Engine — implemented logic, zero coverage (real gaps)\n\n#### 1.1 `should_auto_apply` — `engine/agent/graph.py:40`\nThe auto-apply gate. Named constants exist specifically so eval sweeps them — this is the single most load-bearing function in the system and has no test.\n\n**Edge cases missed**: threshold boundary (`==0.85` should pass, per `>=`), severity boundary (`==2` passes, `==3` fails, per `<=`), and the *conjunction* — high confidence must not override high severity.\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/agent/test_graph.py\nimport pytest\nfrom agent.graph import should_auto_apply, AUTO_APPLY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD, AUTO_APPLY_MAX_SEVERITY\n\ndef test_applies_at_threshold_and_max_severity():\n    assert should_auto_apply(confidence=AUTO_APPLY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD, severity=AUTO_APPLY_MAX_SEVERITY)\n\ndef test_rejects_just_below_confidence_threshold():\n    assert not should_auto_apply(confidence=0.849999, severity=1)\n\ndef test_rejects_severity_above_max_even_at_full_confidence():\n    assert not should_auto_apply(confidence=1.0, severity=3)\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"severity\", [1, 2])\ndef test_applies_for_all_severities_at_or_below_max(severity):\n    assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.9, severity=severity)\n\ndef test_rejects_low_confidence_even_at_low_severity():\n    assert not should_auto_apply(confidence=0.1, severity=1)\n```\n\n#### 1.2 `severity_for_orphan` — `engine/pipeline/detect.py:33`\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_detect.py\nfrom pipeline.detect import severity_for_orphan\n\ndef test_orphan_with_children_is_severity_4():\n    assert severity_for_orphan(has_children=True) == 4\n\ndef test_orphan_without_children_is_severity_3():\n    assert severity_for_orphan(has_children=False) == 3\n```\n\n#### 1.3 `rule_specificity` — `engine/pipeline/schema.py:108`\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_schema.py\nimport pytest\nfrom pipeline.schema import rule_specificity, SurvivorshipRule\n\ndef make_rule(field, entity_type, strategy=\"escalate\", **kw):\n    return SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=field, entity_type=entity_type,\n                             strategy=strategy, description=\"d\", **kw)\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"field,entity_type,expected\", [\n    (\"*\", \"*\", 0),\n    (\"territory\", \"*\", 2),\n    (\"*\", \"account\", 1),\n    (\"territory\", \"account\", 3),\n])\ndef test_specificity_ordering(field, entity_type, expected):\n    assert rule_specificity(make_rule(field, entity_type)) == expected\n```\n\n#### 1.4 `SurvivorshipRule` validator — `engine/pipeline/schema.py:101`\nMissing: the one piece of validation logic that's actually written.\n\n```python\ndef test_prefer_source_without_preferred_source_id_rejected():\n    with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n        SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\",\n                          strategy=\"prefer_source\", description=\"d\")\n\ndef test_prefer_source_with_preferred_source_id_accepted():\n    SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"prefer_source\",\n                      preferred_source_id=\"src-a\", description=\"d\")\n\ndef test_non_prefer_source_strategy_does_not_require_preferred_source_id():\n    SurvivorshipRule(id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"most_recent\", description=\"d\")\n```\n\n#### 1.5 `CanonModel` camelCase boundary — `engine/pipeline/schema.py:51`\nThis *is* the tool contract enforcement mechanism (AGENTS.md: \"do not change one side without changing the other\"). Untested, it can silently drift.\n\n```python\ndef test_canon_model_serializes_camel_case_by_alias():\n    e = CanonicalEntity(external_id=\"a\", entity_type=\"account\", name=\"Acme\",\n                         normalized_name=\"acme\", source_id=\"s1\")\n    dumped = e.model_dump(by_alias=True)\n    assert dumped[\"externalId\"] == \"a\"\n    assert \"external_id\" not in dumped\n\ndef test_canon_model_populates_from_snake_case_kwargs():\n    e = CanonicalEntity(external_id=\"a\", entity_type=\"account\", name=\"Acme\",\n                         normalized_name=\"acme\", source_id=\"s1\")\n    assert e.external_id == \"a\"\n\ndef test_canon_model_rejects_unknown_field():\n    with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n        CanonicalEntity(external_id=\"a\", entity_type=\"account\", name=\"Acme\",\n                         normalized_name=\"acme\", source_id=\"s1\", bogus_field=\"x\")\n```\n\n#### 1.6 Confidence bounds — `Match.confidence`, `Resolution.confidence`\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"bad\", [-0.01, 1.01])\ndef test_match_confidence_out_of_range_rejected(bad):\n    with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n        Match(run_id=uuid4(), entity_a_id=uuid4(), entity_b_id=uuid4(),\n              confidence=bad, method=\"exact_key\",\n              signals=MatchSignals(exact_key=True, cosine=0, fuzzy_ratio=0))\n```\n\n#### 1.7 `POST /runs` — `engine/main.py:31` (the one implemented route)\nNo test exercises it. Missing: happy path, malformed body, and that the background task actually gets scheduled with the right `run_id`.\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/test_main.py\nfrom uuid import uuid4\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom main import app\n\nclient = TestClient(app)\n\ndef test_start_run_returns_run_id_and_accepted():\n    run_id = uuid4()\n    with patch(\"main.execute_run\") as mock_execute:\n        resp = client.post(\"/runs\", json={\"runId\": str(run_id)})\n    assert resp.status_code == 200\n    assert resp.json() == {\"runId\": str(run_id), \"accepted\": True}\n    mock_execute.assert_called_once_with(run_id)\n\ndef test_start_run_rejects_non_uuid_run_id():\n    resp = client.post(\"/runs\", json={\"runId\": \"not-a-uuid\"})\n    assert resp.status_code == 422\n\ndef test_start_run_rejects_missing_body():\n    resp = client.post(\"/runs\", json={})\n    assert resp.status_code == 422\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Web — implemented logic, zero coverage (real gaps)\n\n#### 2.1 `survivorshipRuleSchema` refinement — `web/types/rules.ts:32`\nMirror of engine 1.4 — must be tested on **both** sides since it's a duplicated contract, and the two can drift independently.\n\n```ts\n// web/types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { survivorshipRuleSchema } from \"./rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"prefer_source\",\n      preferredSourceId: \"src-a\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not require preferredSourceId for other strategies\", () => {\n    const result = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      id: \"r1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", strategy: \"most_recent\", description: \"d\",\n    });\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n#### 2.2 `ruleSpecificity` parity with engine — `web/types/rules.ts:52`\nThis is the highest-value integration-shaped test in the repo: if this diverges from `engine/pipeline/schema.py::rule_specificity`, rule evaluation order silently disagrees between layers.\n\n```ts\ndescribe.each([\n  [\"*\", \"*\", 0],\n  [\"territory\", \"*\", 2],\n  [\"*\", \"account\", 1],\n  [\"territory\", \"account\", 3],\n])(\"ruleSpecificity(%s, %s)\", (field, entityType, expected) => {\n  it(`= ${expected}`, () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ field, entityType } as SurvivorshipRule)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n#### 2.3 `reviewActionSchema` discriminated union — `web/types/resolution.ts:34`\nThis gates every human review action; malformed payloads here would previously have been silently coerced.\n\n```ts\nit(\"rejects override without overrideValue\", () => {\n  expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", reviewedBy: \"vzd\" }).success).toBe(false);\n});\nit(\"rejects approve with empty reviewedBy\", () => {\n  expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\", reviewedBy: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n});\nit(\"accepts a valid override\", () => {\n  expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({\n    action: \"override\", reviewedBy: \"vzd\", overrideValue: \"APAC-SOUTH\",\n  }).success).toBe(true);\n});\n```\n\n#### 2.4 `isRunActive` / `TERMINAL_RUN_STATUSES` — `web/types/run.ts:81`\nDrives whether the console keeps polling. A bug here means a completed run polls forever or a running one stops early.\n\n```ts\nit.each([\"queued\", \"extracting\", \"matching\", \"detecting\", \"resolving\"])(\n  \"%s is active\", (status) => expect(isRunActive(status as RunStatus)).toBe(true),\n);\nit.each([\"complete\", \"failed\"])(\n  \"%s is terminal\", (status) => expect(isRunActive(status as RunStatus)).toBe(false),\n);\n```\n\n#### 2.5 `cn()` — `web/lib/cn.ts:4`\n```ts\nit(\"dedupes conflicting tailwind classes, last wins\", () => {\n  expect(cn(\"p-2\", \"p-4\")).toBe(\"p-4\");\n});\nit(\"drops falsy values\", () => {\n  expect(cn(\"a\", false && \"b\", undefined, \"c\")).toBe(\"a c\");\n});\n```\n\n#### 2.6 `SeverityMark` — `web/components/severity-mark.tsx`\nAGENTS.md is explicit: *\"Never render the mark without the word.\"* That's an accessibility invariant with zero enforcement today — a future refactor could silently drop the label and nothing would catch it.\n\n```tsx\n// web/components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"./severity-mark\";\n\nit.each([[4, \"Structural\"], [3, \"Attribute\"], [2, \"Attribute\"], [1, \"Cosmetic\"]])(\n  \"severity %i always renders its label\", (severity, label) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={severity as 1 | 2 | 3 | 4} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(label)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  },\n);\n```\n\n#### 2.7 `NavRail` active-state — `web/components/console/nav-rail.tsx:32`\nUses `pathname.startsWith(item.href)` — correct for sub-routes (`/sources/new` should highlight \"Sources\"), but a latent collision risk if a future top-level route shares a prefix (e.g. a hypothetical `/sources-archive` would also highlight \"Sources\"). Worth locking the intended behavior now.\n\n```tsx\nit(\"highlights parent nav item for a sub-route\", () => {\n  mockUsePathname(\"/sources/new\");\n  render(<NavRail />);\n  expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Sources\" })).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\");\n});\n\nit(\"does not highlight unrelated items\", () => {\n  mockUsePathname(\"/sources/new\");\n  render(<NavRail />);\n  expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Runs\" })).not.toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\");\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Missing error handling tests\n\n| Site | Untested failure mode |\n|---|---|\n| `web/lib/db/index.ts::getDb()` | Throws when `DATABASE_URL` unset — message content untested |\n| `engine/main.py::start_run` | Malformed/missing body → 422 (§1.7 above) |\n| `engine/pipeline/schema.py::SurvivorshipRule` | `prefer_source` without id (§1.4) |\n| `engine/pipeline/schema.py::Match/Resolution` | Out-of-range confidence (§1.6) |\n| `web/types/source.ts::sourceConfigSchema` | Empty `objects` array — `min(1)` untested |\n| `web/types/rules.ts::createRulesetSchema` | Empty `rules` array — `min(1)` untested |\n\n```ts\nit(\"throws with an actionable message when DATABASE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n  vi.stubEnv(\"DATABASE_URL\", \"\");\n  vi.resetModules();\n  const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n  expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n});\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_start_run_rejects_missing_body():  # duplicate of §1.7, listed for completeness\n    ...\n```\n\n```ts\nit(\"rejects a source config with no objects\", () => {\n  expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n});\nit(\"rejects a ruleset with zero rules\", () => {\n  expect(createRulesetSchema.safeParse({ name: \"v1\", rules: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Integration test gaps\n\n1. **Contract parity, Python ↔ TypeScript.** `rule_specificity` (engine) and `ruleSpecificity` (web) are hand-duplicated. There's no automated check they agree. Short of a cross-language test, the closest practical guard is table-driven tests with *identical* input/output fixtures on both sides (§1.3 / §2.2) — keep the parametrize tables byte-identical so a diff in one flags a diff in the other.\n2. **`listSources()` / `countSourcesBySide()` against a real DB** — `web/lib/server/sources.ts`. No test DB is wired up. Needs either a disposable Postgres (Supabase local dev / testcontainers) or a Drizzle mock:\n   ```ts\n   // web/lib/server/sources.test.ts — requires a seeded test DATABASE_URL\n   it(\"countSourcesBySide splits synthetic from crm/warehouse\", async () => {\n     await getDb().insert(sources).values([\n       { name: \"SF\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] } },\n       { name: \"DBX\", kind: \"databricks\", config: { objects: [\"gtm.accounts\"] } },\n       { name: \"Seed\", kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"run42\"] } },\n     ]);\n     expect(await countSourcesBySide()).toEqual({ crm: 1, warehouse: 1, synthetic: 1 });\n   });\n   ```\n3. **Table-ownership enforcement.** AGENTS.md's central invariant (\"engine never writes `sources`/`rulesets`; web never writes `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts`\") has no test anywhere. Once `db.py`'s write functions are implemented, add a static check: engine's Postgres role should lack `INSERT`/`UPDATE` grants on `sources`/`rulesets` at the DB level, verified by an integration test that attempts the write and expects it to be rejected by Postgres, not just by convention.\n4. **End-to-end run flow** (`POST /api/runs` → engine `POST /runs` → status polling) doesn't exist yet on either side — flagged as a Phase 4 dependency, not a current gap.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Stub functions — contract-pinning tests (write now, they'll fail until Phase 2/3 lands)\n\nRather than fabricate behavior for `NotImplementedError` bodies, pin the **documented contract** so implementation has a spec to satisfy (and CI turns red the moment someone forgets a documented edge case). One representative example per module — the pattern repeats for the rest:\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_normalize.py\nclass TestFoldName:\n    \"\"\"Contract, per docstring: deterministic, total, folds case/whitespace/\n    punctuation/legal suffixes ('Inc.', 'Pvt Ltd', 'GmbH'). Currently raises\n    NotImplementedError — un-skip once Phase 2 lands.\"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_folds_case(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"ACME INC\") == fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\")\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_folds_legal_suffix_without_discarding_original(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\") == fold_name(\"Acme\")\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_is_deterministic(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme GmbH\") == fold_name(\"Acme GmbH\")\n```\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_detect.py (extends §1.2)\nclass TestClassify:\n    \"\"\"Per AGENTS.md § Severity Model.\"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_parent_external_id_diff_is_structural_severity_4(self): ...\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_territory_diff_is_attribute_severity_3(self): ...\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_values_folding_to_same_normalized_form_are_cosmetic_severity_1(self): ...\n```\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/agent/test_graph.py (extends §1.1)\nclass TestValidate:\n    \"\"\"NON-NEGOTIABLE per AGENTS.md: rejects any value that isn't observed or a\n    legal normalization of one. This is the ablation the paper measures.\"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 3 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_rejects_a_hallucinated_value_not_in_either_source(self):\n        assert not validate(\"ACC-9999-MADE-UP\", value_a=\"ACC-4417\", value_b=\"ACC-2201\")\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 3 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_accepts_one_of_the_two_observed_values(self):\n        assert validate(\"ACC-4417\", value_a=\"ACC-4417\", value_b=\"ACC-2201\")\n\n    @pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 3 — not yet implemented\")\n    def test_accepts_a_legal_normalization_of_an_observed_value(self):\n        assert validate(\"acme inc\", value_a=\"Acme Inc.\", value_b=\"ACME\")\n```\n\nApply the same `@pytest.mark.skip` pattern to: `block`/`score`/`combine`/`match` (blocking.py), `select_rule` (graph.py — most-specific-first, first-match-wins, `None` on no match), `baseline_exact`/`baseline_rules`, `generate` (seeded reproducibility: same seed → byte-identical output), and `run_system`/`sweep_auto_apply_threshold` (harness.py).\n\n---\n\n### Priority order\n\n1. Wire up `pytest` (engine) and get a decision on Vitest (web) — nothing else is runnable without this.\n2. §1.1, §1.4, §1.5, §1.6 and §2.1–2.4 — implemented logic that's silently untested *right now*, including the two most safety-critical pieces of the whole system (the auto-apply gate, the `prefer_source` validator).\n3. §5 skeletons, `@skip`-marked — cheap to write today, turns Phase 2/3 into TDD instead of write-then-hope.\n4. §4.2/4.3 (DB integration, table-ownership enforcement) once `db.py` is implemented.\n",
